// EXPECT: FAIL
// ERROR_CONTAINS: ANUBIS_UNKNOWN_ATTRIBUTE
// Lead agent 2026-07-27, from GROK-THOTH's day-one stranger pass. An unrecognized attribute used to
// be accepted SILENTLY, which is the worst failure mode a proof-carrying language has.
//
// `#[verifed]` is one letter off `verified`. It checked GREEN while the program silently lost its
// verification lane — the author believes they have a guarantee they do not have. `#[totally_made_up]`
// was equally welcome. An authority mark that does nothing is worse than no mark at all.
//
// The diagnostic names the closest known attribute, because a typo in an authority mark is exactly
// the case this exists for, and "unknown attribute" without a remedy would trade a silent failure
// for an unhelpful wall.
#[verifed]
fn f() -> i64 { return 1; }
fn main() { print(f()); }
